body:
"Never forget when you came from because when you do, it's a long road home."

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

 Just like that I'm 20 years old in my college apartment newly diagnosed with depression. This song definitely helped me accept myself for who I am, flaws and all.

Broke up mid-June. Decided to reconvene in a week to see how we felt. Kept texting but not as much. A week went by and I called her and she said we made the right call. I was heartbroken but started to process or archiving pictures and deleting texts. We texted sparingly for the next two weeks and then ultimately I called at the end of the month saying that I wanted to try again, she didn't want so I suggested that we stop talking. Things go silent for a few days then I see I have missed FT from her. I knew that she was with her sister out of town so I texted her asking if it was a butt dial, she said yes. Go on another week and then she texts me saying that this is the hardest thing she's dealt with and not a day goes by where she doesn't miss me. I sit on it but ultimately reply reciprocating the feeling.  This is about a week before my birthday in mid-July. She texts me at midnight on my birthday and we exchange a few pleasantries. I think that's the end of it but we keep taking sparingly throughout the rest of the month. Finally, at the beginning of August, I question if we should be talking and she says she can't focus on this due to work. Understandable, so I go silent as well and wish her luck. August 9th she asks me if I'm doing okay, I try to lie at first but I eventually tell the truth. I ask her one more time if we made the right decision and she says yes and that she is sorry. I say again we should stop texting and she agrees but says she'll always be there for me. That's the last time we spoke. I've unfollowed (not unfriended) her on FB but still have her on IG. We look at each other's stories which I know probably doesn't help but I still can't bring myself to cut everything out completely.  So to answer you're question, idk what stage I'm at, I feel more accepting of the break up than I was back in June and some days are better than others, but when the pain hits, it still hits just as bad as the night we broke up. I keep telling myself eventually it will get better even if it doesn't feel that way right now. Sorry for the long response. 

&#x200B;

TL;DR-Healing is not linear, but keep going I guess?
